# What must never leave this machine when a deployment is uploaded.
#
# Vercel CLI uploads the working tree, not the commit — so `.gitignore` is not
# enough on its own. Three things in this repository are uncommitted *on purpose*
# and would otherwise be shipped to a build server:
#
#   data/      the owner's live SQLite database and its uploads
#   .secrets/  the write-capable deploy key and known_hosts
#   .tools/    a 100 MB portable Node toolchain used only by the dev laptop
#
# `.env*` is excluded because a local .env is the one file that would carry the
# Neon password into a build. Vercel injects the real values as project
# environment variables instead.
data/
.secrets/
.tools/
.unjess/
artifacts/

.git/
node_modules/
.next/
out/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
scripts/scratch/

# Not needed to build or serve; keeps the upload honest about what is code.
prototype/
docs/
tests/
